{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu8C6kyBWifVBNx3qN7v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or run the rule, so neither has been checked beyond being created.\n\n**Data:** The data view has `timestamp`, `response`, `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.*`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `request`. `response` is a string field, so I used `response.keyword` for grouping and filtering.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-14751b4d Web logs overview\" has four panels and is at `http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-14751b4d-web-logs-overview-9962ee0e918a`. The panels are:\n- Total requests, as a single number.\n- Requests over time, as a line chart.\n- Requests by response code, as a pie chart.\n- Average bytes by extension, as a bar chart.\n\nThe first dashboard call failed because the date-histogram panel needed an explicit time field. I added `timestamp` and it went through.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-14751b4d 5xx spike\" (id `a88d4ac7-e934-4f43-a13a-ff1ea534eff3`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute. It counts documents whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" in the last 5 minutes and fires above 10.\n\nThe rule is **disabled**, because the create tool defaults to that. I haven't enabled it, since you only asked for it to exist. It also has no action attached, so it would record alerts but not notify anyone. Say if you want it enabled or a connector added."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":20052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"output_tokens":530,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id